.TH LUSTRE-CLUSTERHAT.CONF 5 "2026-10-07" "lustre-clusterhat" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
lustre-clusterhat.conf \- settings for lustre-cluster
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/lustre-clusterhat.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR lustre-cluster (8)
reads
.I /etc/lustre-clusterhat.conf
every time it runs.
The file does not exist by default; every setting has a built-in value.
.PP
The file is a shell fragment: one
.IB NAME = value
per line, no spaces around the equals sign, values containing spaces in
quotes, and comments starting with
.BR # .
The same variables set in the environment are overridden by the file.
.PP
Settings marked
.I format
describe what is on the SD cards.
Change them only before
.BR "lustre-cluster servers format" ;
changing them afterwards makes the commands look for targets that are not
there.
.SH SETTINGS
.SS Nodes
.TP
.BR NODES " (default: " "\(dq1 2 3 4\(dq" )
The ClusterHAT slots in use.
.TP
.BR MDS_NODES " (default: " "\(dq1 2\(dq" ", " \fIformat\fR )
The pair of metadata server nodes.
The MGS and MDT0000 are at home on the first, MDT0001 on the second.
.TP
.BR OSS_NODES " (default: " "\(dq3 4\(dq" ", " \fIformat\fR )
The pair of object storage server nodes.
OST0000 is at home on the first, OST0001 on the second.
.TP
.BR NODE_NET " (default: " 172.19.180 )
First three octets of the network between controller, nodes and clients.
Node
.RI p N
is at
.IR NODE_NET . N ,
the controller at
.IR NODE_NET .254.
The ClusterHAT software and the client image are built for the default;
this is here to be read, not changed.
.TP
.BR LNET_IF " (default: " usb0.10 )
Network interface on the nodes that LNet uses.
.SS File system
.TP
.BR FSNAME " (default: " rpifs ", " \fIformat\fR )
Name of the Lustre file system, at most eight characters.
.TP
.BR CLIENT_MNT " (default: " /mnt/lustre )
Where clients mount it.
.TP
.BR SD_DEV " (default: " /dev/mmcblk0 ", " \fIformat\fR )
The SD card as the nodes see it.
.TP
.BR SWAP_SIZE " (default: " 1GiB ", " \fIformat\fR )
Swap partition on every card.
.TP
.BR MGT_SIZE " (default: " 1GiB ", " \fIformat\fR )
Size of the MGS's target.
.TP
.BR MDT_SIZE " (default: " 8GiB ", " \fIformat\fR )
Size of each MDT.
Both MDS cards hold both MDTs.
.TP
.BR OST_SIZE " (default: " 50GiB ", " \fIformat\fR )
Size of each OST.
Both OSS cards hold both OSTs, so a card needs twice this, plus the swap
partition.
.SS Failover
.TP
.BR UMOUNT_TIMEOUT " (default: " 120 )
Seconds a node may take to unmount its targets before it is powered off.
.TP
.BR SYNC_TIMEOUT " (default: " 1200 )
Seconds to wait for a node's mirrors to finish resynchronising before
giving up on moving targets to it.
.SS Clients
.TP
.BR NCLIENTS " (default: " 8 )
Number of client virtual machines.
.TP
.BR VM_MEM " (default: " 512 )
Memory of each client, in MB.
Eight clients of 512 MB fit a controller with 8 GB.
.TP
.BR VM_CPUS " (default: " 1 )
Virtual CPUs of each client.
.TP
.BR VM_BRIDGE " (default: " brint )
Bridge on the controller the clients are attached to.
.TP
.BR VM_IPBASE " (default: " 100 )
Client
.I N
is at
.IR NODE_NET .( VM_IPBASE + N ).
This is fixed in the client image when it is built; changing it here alone
breaks the clients' network.
.SS Throttle
.TP
.BR THROTTLE_BAND " (default: " 20 )
Band, in MB/s, that
.B lustre-cluster throttle on
divides between the OSTs when it is given no figure.
.SS Updates
.TP
.BR UPDATE_REPO " (default: " https://github.com/ablagodarenko/lustre-clusterhat.git )
Repository
.B lustre-cluster update
installs from.
.TP
.BR UPDATE_REF " (default: " main )
Branch, tag or commit it installs when given none.
.SS Paths
.TP
.BR STATE " (default: " /var/lib/lustre-clusterhat )
Where the node root template, the client image and run-time state live.
.TP
.BR NFSROOT " (default: " /var/lib/clusterctrl/nfs )
Where the nodes' root file systems are exported from.
.TP
.BR SSH_KEY " (default: " /root/.ssh/lustre-clusterhat )
Private key the controller uses for nodes and clients.
.SH EXAMPLES
Four clients with more memory each, and a quicker verdict on a node that
will not unmount:
.PP
.RS
.nf
NCLIENTS=4
VM_MEM=1024
UMOUNT_TIMEOUT=60
.fi
.RE
.PP
Larger OSTs for 256 GB cards in the OSS nodes, set before formatting:
.PP
.RS
.nf
OST_SIZE=110GiB
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lustre-cluster (8)
